# Contact Message delivery (docs/adr/0001-contact-message-delivery.md)
#
# Copy to `.env.local` for local development, and set the same variables in the
# Netlify site's environment. None of these is prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_` — the API
# key is a secret and both addresses are the owner's, so a public name would
# inline all three into the client bundle.

# Resend API key. Create one at https://resend.com/api-keys
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# The sender. Must be on a domain verified in Resend, or the provider rejects
# the send. The Visitor's own address is never the sender — it goes in replyTo.
CONTACT_FROM_EMAIL=portfolio@your-verified-domain.com

# Where Contact Messages are delivered. The owner's inbox.
CONTACT_TO_EMAIL=you@example.com

# End-to-end runs send through Resend for real, with CONTACT_TO_EMAIL pointed at
# `delivered@resend.dev` — Resend's test recipient, which confirms the send
# without mail reaching an inbox. The delivery-failure path is driven from the
# browser instead, by submitting an address the action refuses before Resend is
# called (see FORCED_FAILURE_ADDRESS in src/constants/contact.ts).
